{"id":"st2124","designation":"ST 2124","title":"Material Exchange Format — Mapping JPEG XS Codestreams into the MXF Generic Container","state":"active","suite":null,"official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st2124/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st2124/","checked_at":"2026-11-11"},"scope":"This standard specifies the mapping of JPEG XS codestreams, which contain coded still pictures, into the MXF Constrained Generic Container, as specified in SMPTE ST 379-2. This standard specifies the mapping of JPEG XS codestreams as either frame-wrapped, where each JPEG XS codestream is individually mapped into a frame; or clip-wrapped, where a sequence of JPEG XS codestreams is mapped into a clip. This standard defines the KLV coding, the essence container and compression label values and the essence descriptor. This document does not specify mappings for JPEG XS file formats or JPEG XS containers defined in ISO/IEC 21122-3 Annex A to Annex C. This standard defines the data structure at the signal interfaces of networks or storage media. This standard does not define internal storage formats for MXF compliant devices.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"Intellectual Property","page":2},{"level":1,"title":"Introduction","page":2},{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance Notation","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"4 Terms and Definitions","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"5 JPEG XS Mappings","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 General","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"5.2 JPEG XS Coding Summary (Informative)","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"5.3 Application in the MXF Constrained Generic Container","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"5.4 Progressive Frame-based Wrapping","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"5.5 Interlaced Frame-based Wrapping, 2 Fields per KLV Element","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.6 Clip-based Wrapping","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"6 Key-length-value Coding","page":7},{"level":2,"title":"6.1 JPEG XS Picture Element Key","page":7},{"level":3,"title":"6.1.1 General","page":7},{"level":3,"title":"6.1.2 Essence element count — Byte 14","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"6.1.3 Essence element type — Byte 15","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"6.1.4 Essence element number — Byte 16","page":8},{"level":2,"title":"6.2 JPEG XS Picture Element Length","page":8},{"level":2,"title":"6.3 JPEG XS Picture Element Value","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.1 General (informative)","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.2 Frame-wrapped progressive","page":9},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.3 Frame-wrapped interlaced, 2 fields per KLV Element","page":9},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.4 Clip-wrapped","page":9},{"level":1,"title":"7 SMPTE Label Values","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"7.1 Essence Container Label","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"7.2 Picture Essence Coding Label","page":10},{"level":1,"title":"8 Application Issues","page":11},{"level":2,"title":"8.1 General","page":11},{"level":2,"title":"8.2 Application of the KAG and the KLV Fill Item","page":11},{"level":2,"title":"8.3 Index Table Usage","page":11},{"level":2,"title":"8.4 Operational Pattern Usage","page":11},{"level":2,"title":"8.5 Mapping Track Numbers to Generic Container Elements","page":11},{"level":2,"title":"8.6 Essence Container Partitions","page":11},{"level":1,"title":"9 Essence Descriptors","page":12},{"level":2,"title":"9.1 File Descriptor Sets (informative)","page":12},{"level":2,"title":"9.2 JPEG XS Picture SubDescriptor","page":12},{"level":1,"title":"Annex A JPEG XS Coding of Television Signals (normative)","page":15},{"level":1,"title":"Annex B Illustration of the JPEG XS Picture SubDescriptor (informative)","page":-1},{"level":1,"title":"Annex C Color Encoding Metadata (informative)","page":18},{"level":2,"title":"C.1 General","page":18},{"level":2,"title":"C.2 Color Specification as Defined in ISO/IEC 21122-3","page":18},{"level":2,"title":"C.3 Mapping of Color Encoding-Related Information into MXF Descriptors","pag